<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Athamanians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Athamanes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Athamanians were an ancient people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pindus">Pindus</a> mountains in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, living around the upper Achelous between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolia">Aetolia</a>. Usually counted among the Epirote tribes, they were ruled by their own kings and formed a small independent kingdom in the later 3rd and early 2nd centuries BCE, most notably under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amynander">Amynander</a>, before falling under Macedonian and then Roman control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athamanians.jpg" alt="Athamanians" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MaryroseB54 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_ancient_Epirus_and_environs_(English).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
